course: dictionary
lesson: 14520
title: Perforation
level: primary-5
stars: 1
explain: A perforation is a small hole, or one of a line of small holes, made through something. Paper often has perforations so that it can be torn off neatly.
explain: «Tear along the perforation to get your ticket.» The words tear along tell you the holes are there to help the paper split in a straight line. Try your meaning in the sentence: "tear along the small holes to get your ticket" still makes sense, so you have it.
explain: The word can also mean a hole in the body. «The doctor said Kofi had a perforated eardrum, a small hole that usually heals.» Here perforated means "with a hole in it", so the perforation is the hole itself.
fact: Perforation means a small hole, or a line of small holes, made through something.
fact: «Perforations» is the plural, so it means more than one hole.
fact: Perforations on stamps, tickets and toilet roll let you tear along a neat line.
fact: «Perforated» means having holes made in it, as in «a perforated line».
fact: In medicine, a perforation is a hole in a part of the body that should not have one, such as a perforated eardrum, which usually heals.
exercise: «Tear along the perforation to get your ticket.» What is a perforation? | A type of paper | A long crack in a wall | *A small hole, or a line of small holes, that helps paper tear neatly | A loud noise
exercise: «The stamp had neat perforations around its edge.» Perforations is plural. What does it mean here? | Sticky glue | Colourful pictures | *Small holes made in a neat line | Folded corners
exercise: «The doctor said Kofi had a perforated eardrum.» What is a perforation in medicine? | *A hole in a part of the body that should not have one | A type of medicine you swallow | A tune played on a drum | A loud cough
test: What do the perforations on a form help you do? | Read it in the dark | Make it smell nice | *Tear the paper off neatly | Fold it into a paper plane
test: Which is the best meaning of perforation? | A kind of loud bell | *A hole made through something, or a line of small holes | A paper cup | A soft blanket
exam: Which sentence uses perforation correctly? | «The perforations was a happy song.» | «She perforation the sky was blue.» | «She ate a perforation for breakfast.» | *«She tore the stamp along its perforations.»
